Date: Wed, 08 Feb 2012 17:19:04 +0100
Subject: Unable to recover column names from a matrix
Message-ID: <4F83E158-AFFB-4512-86C6-599D189369B3@gmail.com>

I think I've found a bug related to the recovery of column names in matrices.

The following R command generates a matrix with two name columns: b<- as.matrix(data.frame(a=c(1, 2), b=c(1,2)))
Nevertheless, instead of returning a Map with the names and values, RConnection.eval returns a REXPDouble that makes impossible to get the names of the columns.

Hope that helps to improve the package,

Víctor

From simon.urbanek at r-project.org  Thu Feb  9 01:42:33 2012
From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Wed, 08 Feb 2012 20:42:33 -0500
Subject: Re: Unable to recover column names from a matrix
In-Reply-To: <4F83E158-AFFB-4512-86C6-599D189369B3@gmail.com>
References: <4F83E158-AFFB-4512-86C6-599D189369B3@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <4C6FBEC4-6667-4559-AE01-D516C762DDA6@r-project.org>


On Feb 8, 2012, at 11:19 AM, Víctor Pascual Cid wrote:

> I think I've found a bug related to the recovery of column names in matrices.
> 
> The following R command generates a matrix with two name columns: b<- as.matrix(data.frame(a=c(1, 2), b=c(1,2)))
> Nevertheless, instead of returning a Map with the names and values, RConnection.eval returns a REXPDouble that makes impossible to get the names of the columns.
> 

That's not a bug - matrices are vectors, they are not maps. Names on matrices are attributes in R - that's how you get them:

> b<- as.matrix(data.frame(a=c(1, 2), b=c(1,2)))
> attributes(b)
$dim
[1] 2 2

$dimnames
$dimnames[[1]]
NULL

$dimnames[[2]]
[1] "a" "b"


Cheers,
Simon

