From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Thu, 09 Feb 2012 22:59:48 -0500
Subject: Re: How to start JGR as a full sized window?
In-Reply-To: <CADELuTH83FMptuBw+C0wWDCYY7nHS9mfjYGmL6nODy+jSQ+_AA@mail.gmail.com>
References: <CADELuTH83FMptuBw+C0wWDCYY7nHS9mfjYGmL6nODy+jSQ+_AA@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <38DC8F8F-B802-4703-8082-DFCB9F8A7D44@r-project.org>

On Feb 9, 2012, at 12:29 AM, Iurie Malai wrote:

> I want to start JGR as a full sized/maximized window automatically, but how
> to do this? For other applications I can add option "--geometry 1440x900"
> to the launch command, but for JGR this do not work. Sugestions?

There is no command line option, but you an do that from R once it's running:

cons <- J("org.rosuda.JGR.JGR")$MAINRCONSOLE
cons$setExtendedState(cons$MAXIMIZED_BOTH)

(e.g. in your startup files)

Cheers,
Simon

